%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 002b9076b5a919941a76b7b86978d20e, type: 3}
  m_Name: 10_Lina_Arrival
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::Conversation
  showPanel: 0
  panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  panelColor: {r: 0.06, g: 0.07, b: 0.13, a: 1}
  panelTitle: 
  Lines:
  - text: The bell rings. Lina enters carrying a worn square mooncake box tied with
      a faded yellow ribbon.
    npcId: 0
    style: 3
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Lina Chen. How many festivals has it been?
    npcId: 1
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Five. I kept finding reasons not to come home.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: And this year?
    npcId: 1
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: I ran out of reasons that sounded honest.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: She places the empty box on the counter.
    npcId: 0
    style: 3
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: My father left this at my flower shop this morning. He didn't come inside.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: We haven't spoken properly since I left. I want to bring him one of the
      mooncakes he used to make for me. But I never learned the recipe.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Tell us what you do remember.
    npcId: 1
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Red bean paste. I used to steal warm spoonfuls while he was filling the
      molds.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Red bean. A memory she can name without hesitation.
    npcId: 5
    style: 1
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: No salted yolk. I hated the salty centre, so he quietly stopped adding
      one to mine.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Quietly?
    npcId: 1
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Grandfather thought changing a family recipe was disrespectful. Dad never
      argued. He just marked my cakes with a tiny flower so I would know.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Leave the centre empty.
    npcId: 5
    style: 1
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: He also cut back the sugar after I said the filling made my teeth ache.
      I thought he was being stingy.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: It took me years to understand how closely he had been listening.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: And the flower mark?
    npcId: 1
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Osmanthus. He dried petals from the tree outside our house and pressed
      them over the top.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: Red bean. No yolk. Less sugar. Osmanthus.
    npcId: 5
    style: 1
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
  - text: I don't expect one cake to fix five silent years. I only want it to say
      that I'm ready to knock on his door.
    npcId: 4
    style: 0
    speakerName: 
    hidePortrait: 0
    panelImage: {fileID: 0}
